course: dictionary
lesson: 5902
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one you need. The word «Marcel» can be a person's first name, as in «Marcel took the train to Paris to see his cousin.» Here Marcel is a boy, and the context shows it because he takes a train and visits family.
explain: «Her hair had deep, regular waves, a marcel wave from the 1920s.» Waves and hair are the clues, so marcel here is a hairstyle, not a name. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence. A person's name, or a hairstyle? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Marcel can also be a verb, an old-fashioned one: «The hairdresser marcelled her hair before the party.» Marcelled means made deep, regular waves in hair with hot curling irons. Swap in curled and the sentence still works, so your meaning fits. When you are not sure, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: A capital M on Marcel usually means a person's first name.
fact: «Marcel» is a man's first name, especially in France.
fact: Marcel Marceau was a famous French mime artist, who told stories without speaking.
fact: A «marcel wave» is a hairstyle with deep, regular waves, made with hot curling irons, and it was popular in the 1920s.
fact: «Marcelled» is an old-fashioned verb meaning to make such waves in someone's hair.
exercise: «Marcel took the train to Paris to see his cousin.» In this sentence, what is Marcel? | A hot curling iron | A hairstyle | *A man's first name | A kind of wave in the sea
exercise: «Her hair had deep, regular waves, a marcel wave from the 1920s.» What is a marcel wave? | A big wave at the beach | A hot drink | *A hairstyle with deep, regular waves | A dance step
exercise: «The hairdresser marcelled her hair before the party.» Find and copy the word that means made waves in hair. | *marcelled | party | before | hairdresser
test: «Her hair was marcelled for the party.» What does marcelled mean here? | *Had deep waves made in it with hot curling irons | Was dyed bright blue | Was covered by a hat | Was cut very short
test: In French class, Marcel is a name. In a history book, a marcel is a hairstyle. How can you tell which one an author means? | By whether the word starts with a capital letter, always | *By the words around it: people's names come with people, and hairstyles come with hair and waves | By the number of letters in the word | By guessing, because both are equally likely
exam: Which fact about Marcel is true? | Marcel is a Scottish word for a grey, wet day | Marcel always means a hairstyle | *Marcel is usually a person's first name, especially in France | Marcel means very old
